AcuStorm is acupuncture application for professionals, students and amateurs. At the moment application supports Traditional, Five-Element, Meridian Style, Dr. Tan's Balance Method and Master Tung's styles of acupuncture.

All the functionality and content are divided into tabs with the following key features.

Atlas:
- three-layer color figures;
- single, multi-window and full-screen mode;
- zooming and scrolling of figures;
- selecting figures and easy pseudo-3D navigation with a history;
- displaying points and channels in accordance with required filters;
- displaying point combinations in multi-window mode;
- displaying points in the clipboard (an illustration of any texts);
- point pop-up summary;
- dynamic projections (images): select sick area and find its corresponding therapeutic areas.

Points:
- channel and extra points description from Acupuncture: A Comprehensive Text by Shanghai College of Traditional Medicine translated by John O'Connor and Dan Benski;
- channels with the information compiled from several sources;
- channel circuits constructed from the channels related according to 5 types of connections with their indications, functions, illustrations, and application;
- images and mirrors reflecting correspondence between parts of the human body;
- points locations clarified by several reliable textbooks and atlases;
- Master Tung's points compiled from several sources;
- Named Combinations such as composed points, Miriam Lee's Ten Points, Dr. Tan's Smart Combos and 12 Magic Points;
- flat lists of points with bookmarks for fast access;
- searching and filtering of channels and points;
- paging and hyperlinks with history;
- division of information into the toggled sections keeping their state while paging;
- local scalable drawings;
- favorites bookmarks;
- point categories.

Therapy:
- point functions, indications, combinations compiled from several sources;
- chapter "Therapy" from the Acupuncture: A Comprehensive Text;
- body areas with the passing channels, balancing channels according to Dr. Tan, correponding images, homological anatomical structures, acupuncture points targeting to these areas;
- searching and filtering of functions, indications, combinations, conditions;
- flat lists with bookmarks and filters for fast access;
- paging and hyperlinks with history;
- displaying point combinations in the atlas in multi-window mode;
- division of information into the toggled sections keeping their state while paging;
- user notes with possibility to display their points in atlas;
- favorites bookmarks.

General:
- acupuncture styles with AcuStorm;
- point categories;
- locating the points;
- bibliography.

In addition:
- Balance Assistant - dynamic matrix which helps to select balancing channels for a set of affected channels;
- useful links to appropriate Internet resources with video, figures, text information arranged in a corresponding context;
- short help for each section.

Settings:
- selecting points nomenclature for displaying (WHO, English, French, etc.);
- optional displaying point, channel and vessel names;
- selecting point location if different sources specify it differently;
- adjusting number of atlas windows.

Shop:
- division of functionality and content into separate modules, you can choose the ones you need;
- trying modules during a week;
- buying modules for the coins from your balance;
- recharging your balance through AppStore purchases.
